# AU DIC Benchmark Evaluation Framework — Implementation Plan (Sprint 003)

## Overview
With **Sprint 001** (Framework Subsystem), **Sprint 002** (Field Evaluators & Normalizers), **Confidence Calibration**, and **Error Taxonomy Engine** fully implemented and verified (100% test pass rate), we now move into **Sprint 003: Quality Profile Robustness & Degradation Penalty Evaluation**.

Sprint 003 evaluates AU DIC accuracy decay across physical acquisition degradations:
- `clean` (Digital vector rendering baseline)
- `scanner_copy` (Scan blur, contrast drop, binarization noise)
- `mobile_camera` (Perspective distortion, shadow gradient, lens flare)
- `rotated_90` (Exact 90° clockwise page rotation)

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Quality Profile Robustness Analysis Policy**:
> - Evaluates document processing performance decay curves across `clean` $\to$ `scanner_copy` $\to$ `mobile_camera` $\to$ `rotated_90`.
> - Calculates profile degradation penalties ($\Delta \text{F1}$, $\Delta \text{CER}$, $\Delta \text{Accuracy}$) relative to the digital vector baseline (`clean`).

